{"strongs": "H6113", "word": "עָצַר", "translit": "a.tsar", "root": "עצר", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "restrain, retain", "definition": "עָצַר 46 verb restrain, retain (Late Hebrew id. ; compare probably Assyrian eƒêru , retain, restrain , Dl HWB 122 Jäger BAS i. 483 Zehnpf ib. 500 ; Ethiopic press , Arabic ; ᵑ7 עֲצַר Syriac id. ); ** compare Assyrian usƒurtu , taboo SAC JA, 1904, 754 . — Qal Perfect 3 masculine singular ׳ ע Gen 20:18 +, suffix עֲצָרַנִי Gen 16:2 1 singular יָצַרְתִּי Dan 10:8 ; Dan 10:16 etc.; Imperfect 3 masculine singular יַעְצֹר 1Sam 9:17 +, יַעְצָרֿ 2Chr 2:5 suffix יַעֲצָרְכָה 1Kgs 18:44 , etc.; Infinitive absolute עָצֹר Gen 20:18 , construct לַעִצֹר 2Chr 22:9 , וַעְצֹר Job 4:2 ( Ges «GKC:28b»§ 28b ); Passive participle עָצוּר Jer 33:1 +, etc.; — 1. restrain , with accusative of person Gen 16:2 ( J ; + מִן , i.e. prevent), עָצֹר עָצַר בְּעֵד כָּלרֶֿחֶם Gen 20:18 ( E ), compare absolute Isa 66:9 (opposed to מוֺלִיד ); followed by infinitive 2Kgs 4:24 with accusative of person alone 1Kgs 18:44 hinder, stop ; with accusative of sky (hindering rain) Deut 11:17 ; 2Chr 7:13 passive participle absolute shut up , or hindered (for reasons not given) Jer 36:5 ; Neh 6:10 (? by a vow, or by ceremonial uncleanness, compare Rs Sem i. 436 f., 2nd ed. 455 f. ); = shut up (with ב , in prison) 2Kgs 17:4 , passive participle Jer 33:1 ; Jer 39:15 , figurative Jer 20:9 on עָצוּר וְעָזוּב (5 t.) see I. עזב ; עֲצֻרָה לָנוּ 1Sam 21:6 women have been kept away with reference to us (compare RS l.c .); עָצוּר מִפְּנֵי 1Chr 12:1 kept away from before Saul; = detain , with accusative Judg 13:15 ; Judg 13:16 in Job with בְּ , בְּמִלִּין ׳ ע Job 4:2 , compare Job 29:9 , so בַּמַּיִם Job 12:5 בְּעַמִּי ׳ ע 1Sam 9:17 is rule over , etc. (si vera lectio); insert also (with other words) 1Sam 10:1 ᵐ5 We Dr and others 2. (late) retain , with accusative כֹּחַ 2Chr 13:20 ; 2Chr 22:9 ; Dan 10:8 ; Dan 10:16 ; Dan 11:6 + infinitive = be able to 1Chr 29:14 ; 2Chr 2:5 omit כֹּחַ 2Chr 14:10 (+ עִמְּךָ ), 2Chr 20:37 (+ infinitive). Niph`al be restrained, stayed , of plague: Perfect 3 feminine singular נֶעֱצָ֑רָה Num 17:15 Imperfect 3 feminine singular תֵּעָצַר 2Sam 24:27 = 1Chr 21:22 , וַתֵּעָצַר Num 17:13 ; Num 25:8 ( P ) 2Sam 24:25 ; Ps 106:30 be shut up (of sky), Infinitive construct בְּהֵעָצֵר 1Kgs 8:35 = 2Chr 6:26 be under restraint or detention Participle נֶעְצָר 1Sam 21:8 + ׳ לִפְחנֵי י (? i.e. kept by a vow, compare HPS and Neh 6:10 above).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6302')\">BDB6302</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H6113')\">H6113</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6301')\">BDB6301</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6303')\">BDB6303</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>עָצַר</bdbheb><sub>46</sub> <b>verb</b> <highlightword>restrain, retain</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>; compare probably Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>eƒêru</highlight></transliteration>, <highlight>retain, restrain</highlight>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dl')\">Dl<sup>HWB 122</sup></lookup> Jäger<sup>BAS i. 483</sup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Zehnpf')\">Zehnpf<sup>ib. 500</sup></lookup>; Ethiopic <placeholder4022/> <highlight>press</highlight>, Arabic <placeholder4023/>; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <bdbheb>עֲצַר</bdbheb> Syriac <placeholder4024/> <highlight>id.</highlight>); <div class=\"remarks\"><b>**</b>compare Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>usƒurtu</highlight></transliteration>, <highlight>taboo</highlight> SAC<sup>JA, 1904, 754</sup>. — </div><div class=\"point\"><b>Qal</b> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> 3 masculine singular <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ע</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 20:18\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(1,20,18)\">Gen 20:18</ref> +, suffix <bdbheb>עֲצָרַנִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 16:2\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"b